**Source-set finding (SF-1).** SAEOS-1 §6.1b names six emission sources: L06 trade-off matrix,
L04 candidate set, L08 architecture artifact set, L11 implementation contract, decision-graph
records, scar-graph. **For all three goals, five of those six do not exist as artifacts.** What
exists is the L17 close-out pair (`docs/*-constitutional-review.md` + `reviews/tasks/*_review.md`)
plus the L15 Atlas row and the CER-3 debt records. Extraction is therefore an attack on the
*retrospective*, not on a decision record — and a retrospective is written to justify, not to
enumerate alternatives. This shapes every result below.

**Deliberate inclusion of `reviews/tasks/*_review.md`.** The 10-point protocol form
(`operations/IMPLEMENTATION_REVIEW_PROTOCOL.md` §2) contributed **near-zero** extractable
content beyond `status`. Its cells are `Status: PASS` + one sentence. It is a *conformance
attestation*, not a knowledge artifact. All real yield came from the `docs/` CER-4 six-question
form and from `ledger/debt/`. Recorded here because `S-PROBE` names `reviews/tasks/` as the
source and the honest answer is that it is the weaker half of the pair.

