## §3 Scoring method

**Verdicts.** `extractable` (E) — the field is recoverable by a deterministic rule from source
text, no synthesis. `partial` (P) — recoverable only by inference, generation, or with a named
sub-field missing. `absent` (A) — no source text bears on it. `n/a` — the goal genuinely had no
instance of that node type (e.g. no failure occurred, so no `Scar` exists); **excluded from the
denominator**, because scoring "nothing bad happened" as extraction loss would manufacture a
falsification.

**Universe.** Per goal: the 17 leaf fields of the §4.2 universal envelope (scored once per
goal — envelope extraction is uniform across node types emitted from one artifact set, since
it draws on the same document metadata), plus 40 type-specific content fields distributed
across the 12 §4.3 types.

**Formula.**

```
loss_ratio = ( |absent| + 0.5 · |partial| ) / ( |extractable| + |partial| + |absent| )
```

`partial` at 0.5 is the load-bearing convention. Justification: a `partial` field is one an
extractor *can* fill but only by generating text no human ratified — which under
`ENGINEERING_LIFECYCLE.md` global rule 3 and CER-6 is un-derived content. Half-credit treats
it as neither free nor fatal. Sensitivity is reported in §6.

